---
import ToolShell from '../../components/ToolShell.astro';
import { u } from '../../utils/url';
---

<ToolShell
  slug="motor-minimum-insulation-resistance"
  title="Motor Minimum Insulation Resistance Check (IEEE 43)"
  description="Free calculator: find the minimum acceptable insulation resistance for a motor or generator winding per IEEE 43, corrected to 40°C, and check your megger reading against it."
  h1="Motor Minimum Insulation Resistance Check"
  intro="Pick the winding type and rated voltage, enter your reading and temperature, and see whether it clears the IEEE 43 recommended minimum."
>
  <Fragment slot="inputs">
    <div class="tool-field"><label for="type">Winding type</label>
      <select id="type">
        <option value="old">Older windings (before about 1970), field windings, others</option>
        <option value="form">Form-wound, built after about 1970 (AC) and DC armatures</option>
        <option value="rand">Random-wound stator coils, or form-wound below 1 kV</option>
      </select></div>
    <div class="tool-field"><label for="kv">Rated line voltage</label>
      <div class="input-wrap"><input id="kv" type="number" min="0" step="any" value="0.415" inputmode="decimal" /><span class="unit">kV</span></div>
      <div class="chips">
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-set='{"kv":0.415}'>415 V</button>
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-set='{"kv":3.3}'>3.3 kV</button>
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-set='{"kv":6.6}'>6.6 kV</button>
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-set='{"kv":11}'>11 kV</button>
      </div></div>
    <div class="tool-split">
      <div class="tool-field"><label for="ir">Measured IR, 1 min</label><div class="input-wrap"><input id="ir" type="number" min="0" step="any" value="30" inputmode="decimal" /><span class="unit">MΩ</span></div></div>
      <div class="tool-field"><label for="temp">Winding temp</label><div class="input-wrap"><input id="temp" type="number" min="-20" max="150" step="any" value="30" inputmode="decimal" /><span class="unit">°C</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="readout">
    <div class="lcd"><small>MIN</small><span id="min">-</span><span class="u">MΩ at 40°C</span></div>
    <div class="lcd-sub" id="detail"></div>
    <div id="verdict"></div>
    <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" id="bar" style="width:0"></div><i class="bar-min" id="bar-min"></i></div>
    <div class="scale-ticks"><span>Your reading at 40°C</span><span>White line: minimum</span></div>
    <div class="lcd-sub" id="volt"></div>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>The IEEE 43 minimums (at 40°C, 1 minute)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Older windings, field windings, others:</strong> rated kV + 1 MΩ.</li>
    <li><strong>Form-wound AC and DC armature windings built after about 1970:</strong> 100 MΩ.</li>
    <li><strong>Random-wound stator coils, and form-wound coils rated below 1 kV:</strong> 5 MΩ.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your reading is first corrected to 40°C with the halving rule (see the <a href={u('/tools/ir-temperature-correction-calculator/')}>temperature correction calculator</a>), then compared with the minimum.</p>
  <h2>Important</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This is a recommended minimum for an in-service machine, not a guarantee of health. A pass with a falling trend still deserves attention.</li>
    <li>Your plant or customer specification may set a higher limit. Always use the stricter one.</li>
    <li>The suggested test voltage shown is a general guide for the rated voltage. Check the machine's own instructions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Related: <a href={u('/blog/how-to-test-motor-windings/')}>how to test motor windings</a> and the <a href={u('/blog/motor-insulation-testing-schedule/')}>motor insulation testing schedule</a>.</p>

  <p>Report template: <a href={u('/templates/#insulation-resistance-test-report')}>Excel insulation resistance test report</a> with the minimums, PI and DAR built in.</p>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); }, C = window.CIE;
      function testV(kv) {
        if (kv < 1) return '500 V DC';
        if (kv <= 2.5) return '500 to 1000 V DC';
        if (kv <= 5) return '1000 to 2500 V DC';
        if (kv <= 12) return '2500 to 5000 V DC';
        return '5000 to 10000 V DC';
      }
      function calc() {
        var type = $('type').value, kv = C.val('kv'), ir = C.val('ir'), t = C.val('temp');
        if (!isFinite(kv) || kv <= 0 || !isFinite(ir) || !isFinite(t) || ir < 0) {
          C.num($('min'), null); $('bar').style.width = '0'; $('detail').textContent = 'Enter valid numbers.'; $('verdict').innerHTML = ''; $('volt').textContent = ''; return;
        }
        var min = type === 'old' ? kv + 1 : type === 'form' ? 100 : 5;
        var f = Math.pow(2, (t - 40) / 10), c = ir * f;
        C.num($('min'), min, function (v) { return C.fmt(v, 3); });
        var sc = Math.max(c, min) * 1.25; $('bar').style.width = (c / sc * 100) + '%'; $('bar').style.background = c >= min ? '#10b981' : '#ef4444'; $('bar-min').style.left = (min / sc * 100) + '%';
        $('detail').innerHTML = 'Your <b>' + C.fmt(ir) + ' MΩ</b> at ' + t + '°C equals <b>' + C.fmt(c) + ' MΩ</b> at 40°C (factor ' + C.fmt(f, 3) + ').';
        $('verdict').innerHTML = c >= min ? C.badge('v-great', 'Meets the minimum') : C.badge('v-bad', 'Below the minimum');
        $('volt').textContent = 'Suggested test voltage for ' + kv + ' kV: ' + testV(kv) + '.';
      }
      ['type', 'kv', 'ir', 'temp'].forEach(function (id) { $(id).addEventListener('input', calc); });
      calc();
    })();
  </script>
</ToolShell>
